        "falseColor": true,
        "qualification": "USGS MOLA global DEM, from Mars Global Surveyor laser measurements in 1999–2001. Heights are meters above the GMM-2B areoid, truncated to degree and order 50. Native spacing is about 463 m; the publisher interpolated gaps. The areoid is a gravity-based reference surface, not a fixed-radius sphere.",
        "notes": "Mars has no global ocean. Its reference level, called the areoid, follows gravity and plays a role similar to sea level on Earth. Meters above the GMM-2B areoid. Blue is lower and warm colors are higher; negative values are below the reference level. Mars Global Surveyor’s MOLA laser measured the surface in 1999–2001. USGS assembled the elevation grid. The source spacing is about 463 m, and the publisher filled gaps by interpolation. This globe shows a coarser sample of that grid. Gray grid marks missing source data.",
